version: research-2026.10.1
message: "If you use results, software, or data from this research repository, cite the specific paper/result where available and cite this repository for the research corpus and verification infrastructure."
title: "BGS: arithmetic quantum chaos and spectral universality"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Churilov
    given-names: Maksim
repository-code: "https://github.com/ChurilovMaksim/BGS"
url: "https://github.com/ChurilovMaksim/BGS"
abstract: >-
  Long-horizon research corpus on rigorous routes to the
  Bohigas-Giannoni-Schmit conjecture for arithmetic and nonlinear quantum
  maps, including proofs, exact reductions, formal finite kernels,
  reproducible verification, counterexamples, retractions, and a consolidated
  research manuscript. Microscopic fixed-strength BGS remains open.
keywords:
  - quantum chaos
  - Bohigas-Giannoni-Schmit conjecture
  - cat maps
  - random matrix theory
  - spectral statistics
  - Weyl quantization
  - arithmetic dynamics
license: MIT
